<h2 id="integration-heading">Pallet Conveyor Integration</h2>
<h3>Palletizer Integration</h3>
<p>Pallet conveyors transport empty pallets to <a href="/industries/packaging-line-conveyors/pallet/">palletizers</a> and loaded pallets away. <a href="/industries/packaging-line-conveyors/pallet/pallet-dispenser/">Pallet dispensers</a> feed empty pallets onto the infeed conveyor. Outfeed conveyors transport loaded pallets to stretch wrap and shipping. Conveyor height must match palletizer load/unload height (typically 16-24" floor to roller top).</p>
<h3>Stretch Wrapper Integration</h3>
<p>Pallet conveyors feed stretch wrappers and remove wrapped pallets. Turntable wrappers require a pallet transfer to position the pallet on the turntable. Rotary arm and ring wrappers allow in-line pallet flow without transfer. Conveyor speed must match wrapper cycle time.</p>
<h3>AS/RS Integration</h3>
<p>Automated storage and retrieval systems (AS/RS) interface with pallet conveyors at pick/deposit stations. Conveyors queue pallets for crane pickup and receive pallets from crane deposits. Zone accumulation controls pallet flow to match crane cycle. Pallet verification (dimensions, weight, label) often occurs on the conveyor before AS/RS entry.</p>
<h3>Dock Operations</h3>
<p>Pallet conveyors transport pallets between production/storage and shipping docks. Gravity pallet flow lanes stage pallets in order. Powered conveyors extend into truck trailers for automated trailer loading systems (ATLS). Dock levelers and vehicle restraints integrate with <a href="/industries/mining-conveyors/">conveyor safety systems</a>.</p>
<h2 id="faq-heading">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<div class="usa-accordion usa-accordion--bordered usa-accordion--multiselectable" data-allow-multiple="">
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="faq-1">What is a pallet conveyor?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-1" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>A pallet conveyor is a heavy-duty conveyor designed to transport loaded pallets (typically 2,000-10,000 lbs). Pallet conveyors use <a href="/conveyor-types/cdlr-conveyors/">CDLR</a>, <a href="/conveyor-types/chain-conveyors/">drag chain</a>, or heavy-duty roller systems. They integrate with <a href="/industries/packaging-line-conveyors/pallet/">palletizers</a>, stretch wrappers, and AS/RS systems.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-2">What type of conveyor is used for pallets?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-2" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>The most common types are <a href="/conveyor-types/cdlr-conveyors/">CDLR</a> for standard pallets up to 10,000 lbs, <a href="/conveyor-types/chain-conveyors/">drag chain</a> for heavy or non-standard pallets, <a href="/conveyor-types/roller-conveyors/gravity/">heavy-duty gravity roller</a> for pallet flow, and <a href="/conveyor-types/transfer-conveyors/">turntables or chain transfers</a> for direction changes. CDLR is the standard for most applications.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-3">How much weight can a pallet conveyor handle?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-3" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>Standard <a href="/conveyor-types/cdlr-conveyors/">CDLR conveyors</a> handle 2,000-4,000 lb pallets. Heavy-duty CDLR and <a href="/conveyor-types/chain-conveyors/">drag chain</a> handle up to 10,000-20,000 lbs. Capacity depends on roller diameter, spacing, bearing rating, chain size, and frame construction. Always specify maximum expected load plus safety factor.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-4">What is the difference between CDLR and drag chain?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-4" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p><a href="/conveyor-types/cdlr-conveyors/">CDLR</a> uses chain-driven rollers that contact pallet bottom boards. Works best with standard pallets. <a href="/conveyor-types/chain-conveyors/">Drag chain</a> uses chain strands that directly contact pallet stringers. Handles block pallets, non-standard sizes, and very heavy loads better than CDLR.</p>

</div>
</div>
